  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1226 AM CST Tue Nov 3 2026\n\nAs of 12:30 AM CST, temperatures across the area are in the upper \n40s to low 50s with winds out of the north at 15 to 20 mph, gusting \nbetween 25 and 35 mph with some locally higher wind gusts noted\naround Pierre. These gusts are expected to last through the day. \nPortions of central SD may see some wind gusts as high as 45 mph \nthrough the morning. Rain showers will also continue through most \nof the day today and through most of Wednesday for northeast SD \nand west central MN. Accumulations across northeast SD have ranged\nbetween 1 and 3 inches already, highest across east central SD, \nparticularly around the Watertown area. The chance of an \nadditional inch of accumulation or more through Wednesday is \naround 50 to 70% mainly east of the James River and highest along \nI-29.\n\nTemperatures through the period will be closer to average than the \nlast week or so with highs in the 40s east of the Missouri River and \nin the low 50s west. Models are starting to show a warm up back into \nthe mid to upper 50s across the entire area for next weekend into \nthe beginning of next work week. Winds Wednesday afternoon behind \nthe low are expected to gust between 30 and 35 mph across the \nmajority of the forecast area. These gusts will die off during the \nevening and into the overnight except for on the eastern slope of \nthe Prairie Coteau of northeast SD.",
